{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-18T11:09:40.162Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"928e5cd9a3bda9591c204f9f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-9x9drr","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-9x9drr","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-43p2c3+pm-5kfzjh+pm-9x9drr+pm-gh1749","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-9x9drr","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-9x9drr","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.327","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-18T11:09:40.162Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-18T11:09:40.162Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implemented in PR 1752. runExtensionExploreManageAction calls prepareExploreManageState(ctx, settings), which runs readAndAdoptExploreManageState (read managed state, list installed packages, adopt unmanaged ones) under withExtensionInstallLock only when manage adopts (--fix-managed-state). refreshManagedExtensionUpdates then runs after the lock is released. requiresExtensionStateLock no longer wraps manage --fix-managed-state at dispatch; doctor --fix-managed-state is unchanged. Nothing after adoption writes state: the second inventory listing, the runtime probe and triage only read. Test: tests/integration/extensions/manage-lock-scope.integration.spec.ts runs manage --fix-managed-state with a stalled npm on PATH, waits until the lookup has started, and acquires the scope lock with a single attempt, which succeeds. Negative control: moving the refresh back inside the lock makes that acquisition fail.\n"}]}],"before_hash":"a933c995855f63cabb432566d20bcc0a94aa7b1f13f70a281035c8a4c5297e18","after_hash":"98dd076099d8ce853af1450c2c643dd8b27f57c1c44165ebbd19b3587674ff94","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"2631b63c2383da21a0d56b09aa55071d8b846cf8936cd2c3d64d21b12654d74a"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-18T11:24:31.420Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"928e5cd9a3bda9591c204f9f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-9x9drr","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-9x9drr","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-43p2c3+pm-5kfzjh+pm-9x9drr+pm-gh1749","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-9x9drr","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-9x9drr","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.327","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-18T11:24:31.419Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implementation attempt on PR 1752 (67c7eef6b), reverted in the next commit. Codex review round 4 found two requirements that moving the lock alone does not meet, so this item stays open for its own change:\n1. Freshness snapshot consistency. Once the lock is released after adoption, a concurrent install can upgrade a package while its remote check runs. The second inventory scan then pairs the new manifest with update evidence computed from the old managed record, so a package just upgraded to latest can still be reported as having an update available. The fix must report one consistent snapshot, for example by re-reading managed state after the refresh and keeping update evidence only for entries whose installed identity (source, manifest_version, updated_at) is unchanged. A concurrently changed entry should report not checked rather than stale evidence.\n2. Host-error boundary. withExtensionInstallLock runs its body inside withHostEnvironmentBoundary, which turns EACCES and EMFILE from readdir into the stable, path-redacted refusal. Moving the inventory scan outside the lock also moved it outside that boundary, so it would reject with a raw Node error that carries the local path. The unlocked diagnostics need their own boundary.\nThe reverted design is still the right starting point: read state, list and adopt under the lock (readAndAdoptExploreManageState); refresh outside it; drop manage from requiresExtensionStateLock. Its test, which acquired the scope lock in one attempt while a stalled npm on PATH was running, and the negative control, which moved the refresh back under the lock and made the acquisition fail, both worked. Reuse them.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-18T11:24:31.420Z"}],"before_hash":"98dd076099d8ce853af1450c2c643dd8b27f57c1c44165ebbd19b3587674ff94","after_hash":"77d6a7b4308d7057b9330f62b08a002876d594edaa42824f795cdc351ea8d692","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ffaded8117a70ba0736dc4cca92743ff082dd006b52508c611ab4c9899649fa5"}
