{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-18T12:31:48.473Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"928e5cd9a3bda9591c204f9f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.327","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-18T12:31:48.473Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Mitigation shipped in PR 1752 while this item stays open: PM_EXTENSION_UPDATE_CHECK_TIMEOUT_MS is clamped to at most 25000 ms, below the 30-second lock wait (EXTENSION_INSTALL_LOCK_ATTEMPTS 120 times EXTENSION_INSTALL_LOCK_DELAY_MS 250). A single lookup batch under the manage --fix-managed-state lock therefore cannot outlast a concurrent install, uninstall or adoption. Several batches (more than four managed npm or GitHub packages, at the concurrency of 4) can still exceed it at the default budget. That is pre-existing and is what this item's structural fix, with the two requirements recorded in the previous comment, must remove.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-18T12:31:48.473Z"}],"before_hash":"195d2b890b0adffedb1486b6c07e054d3b4dd3de0c84db65a60367955878d72d","after_hash":"f135a24c21e05afd768eb3706d5f4f70d3818a46eff02fde2d6cdd192d5f2d82","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"5a5359424757fb99f4265ea88ab2f4507ae7e7f54d47419332c5c644ec9d4d28"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-18T13:00:19.323Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"928e5cd9a3bda9591c204f9f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.327","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-18T13:00:19.323Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Raised by CodeRabbit and Codex on PR 1752 (src/sdk/extension.ts, the prepareExploreManageState path). With --fix-managed-state, dispatchExtensionAction wraps the whole manage handler in withExtensionInstallLock. That handler adopts unmanaged packages and then calls refreshManagedExtensionUpdates, so the lock stays held while every npm view and git ls-remote runs, four at a time. The refresh never persists its result, so it does not need the lock. The lock wait is 30 seconds (120 attempts of 250 ms). As an interim mitigation, PR 1752 makes manage --fix-managed-state ignore PM_EXTENSION_UPDATE_CHECK_TIMEOUT_MS and keep the 10-second default, while the override (clamped to 25 seconds) applies everywhere else. At that default, more than eight managed npm or GitHub packages (three or more batches at concurrency four) can still keep the lock past a concurrent install, uninstall or adopt's 30-second wait, which then fails with a lock conflict. Proposed: keep only the adoption read and write under the lock, and run the refresh and runtime probe after it is released, while meeting the two design requirements recorded in this item's comments: a consistent freshness snapshot, and the host-error boundary."}],"before_hash":"f135a24c21e05afd768eb3706d5f4f70d3818a46eff02fde2d6cdd192d5f2d82","after_hash":"829042facbb07b3366c1916d2d38f36567cbf4f52311f8b504560ea6da80adad","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"079bf66c1a3782592a7572607059ceede649cbfbea258d35e23ba5812792f53e"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-18T13:00:20.957Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"928e5cd9a3bda9591c204f9f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.327","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-18T13:00:20.956Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Reproduction cases (from CodeRabbit on PR 1752):\n- Pre-existing, at the default budget: nine or more managed remote packages make three batches at concurrency four. If every lookup stalls, the refresh holds the lock for about 30 s or more, past a concurrent action's 30-second wait.\n- Introduced and then neutralised in PR 1752: with five managed remote packages (two batches), a raised PM_EXTENSION_UPDATE_CHECK_TIMEOUT_MS of 25000 would have made the locked refresh take about 50 s, against about 20 s at the old fixed budget, turning a concurrent action that used to succeed into a lock conflict. PR 1752 prevents this by keeping the 10-second default for manage --fix-managed-state. The integration test asserts update_check_timeout_ms 10000 there with the override set to 2000.\nOnce this item moves the refresh out of the lock, the override can apply to --fix-managed-state as well.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-18T13:00:20.957Z"}],"before_hash":"829042facbb07b3366c1916d2d38f36567cbf4f52311f8b504560ea6da80adad","after_hash":"c6e42ba37a1b10ce07fa311ca5f84bf4b86ea596f7a96090764c52b1381e0dfa","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d64a774bf94833cdc62e054e203fa67cd2c0541e868a66e1deea9fa8de297483"}
